    *   Complexity: $O(t)$ time, $O(1)$ space. This is efficient enough.

    *   $x, y, n \le 10^9$.
    *   $n-y \le 10^9$.
    *   $m = (n-y)/x \le 10^9$.
    *   $k = m \cdot x + y \le 10^9$.
    *   Standard 32-bit integer (signed) might overflow if the intermediate calculation $m \cdot x$ is done without care, but since $k \le n \le 10^9$, we can safely use 64-bit integers for all calculations to be safe. In Python, integers are arbitrary precision, so no overflow issue. In C++, use `long long`.

